  "quote-to-cash": {
    "status": "published",
    "meta": {
      "slug": "quote-to-cash",
      "title": "Quote to Cash",
      "tier": "core",
      "description": "Optimize quote-to-cash process end-to-end.",
      "status": "published",
      "competencyIds": [],
      "loomEmbedId": "dcbcfbcb84fd4c0dae37cf82adf4af09"
    },
    "advisory": "# Quote-to-Cash — Advisory\n\n> **PLACEHOLDER** — This content is under development.\n\n## Project Overview\n\n### What is Quote-to-Cash?\n\n**Definition:** [Placeholder] A GTM execution project that addresses a specific operational gap in the go-to-market motion. This playbook provides a structured framework for scoping, planning, and executing the Quote-to-Cash initiative.\n\n**What it is NOT:** Not a one-time exercise. Not a tool implementation alone. Not a strategy document without operational backing.\n\n### What Quote-to-Cash Unlocks\n\n| Before | After |\n|--------|-------|\n| Manual processes | Automated workflows |\n| Inconsistent execution | Standardized playbook |\n| Unclear ownership | Defined RACI |\n| No measurement | KPI tracking |\n\n### Business Outcomes\n\n**Primary Outcomes:**\n- Improved operational efficiency across GTM teams\n- Measurable impact on pipeline and revenue metrics\n- Reduced manual effort and human error\n- Clear ownership and accountability\n\n**Secondary Outcomes:**\n- Better cross-functional alignment\n- Foundation for future automation\n- Data-driven decision making\n\n### Who Owns It\n\n**Typical Owner:** Head of RevOps or VP Sales\n\n**Key Stakeholders:**\n- **Executive Sponsor** — Owns outcomes and budget\n- **RevOps Manager** — Technical implementation owner\n- **Sales/Marketing Leadership** — Validates requirements\n- **IT/Security** — Approves integrations\n\n### Prerequisites\n\n- CRM system in place (Salesforce or HubSpot)\n- Defined GTM lifecycle stages\n- Executive sponsorship secured\n- Data access and permissions confirmed\n",
    "methodology": "# Quote-to-Cash — Methodology\n\n> **PLACEHOLDER** — This content is under development.\n\n## Part 1: Discovery & Data Audit\n\n### Step 1: Stakeholder Interviews\n\n**Step Overview:** Conduct structured interviews with key stakeholders to understand current state, pain points, and desired outcomes.\n\n**Who to Interview:**\n- Executive sponsor (CRO, VP Sales, VP Marketing)\n- RevOps Manager / team\n- Sales leadership\n- Marketing operations\n- Customer Success leadership\n\n**Questions to Ask:**\n- What does the current process look like today?\n- Where are the biggest bottlenecks?\n- What tools are currently in use?\n- What does \"good\" look like in 6 months?\n- What has been tried before and why did it fail?\n\n### Step 2: Current State Assessment\n\n**Step Overview:** Document the existing process, tools, data quality, and gaps before designing the solution.\n\n- Map current workflow end-to-end\n- Identify manual steps that can be automated\n- Audit data quality in relevant CRM objects\n- Document tool integrations and data flows\n- Quantify time spent on manual processes\n\n### Step 3: Gap Analysis\n\n| Area | Current State | Target State | Gap |\n|------|--------------|-------------|-----|\n| Process | [Document] | [Define] | [Identify] |\n| Data | [Audit] | [Clean] | [Quantify] |\n| Tools | [Inventory] | [Optimize] | [Evaluate] |\n| People | [Map] | [Train] | [Plan] |\n\n## Part 2: Solution Design\n\n### Step 4: Define Requirements\n\n- Functional requirements (what the solution must do)\n- Non-functional requirements (performance, security, scale)\n- Integration requirements (which systems connect)\n- Reporting requirements (what metrics to track)\n\n### Step 5: Select Approach\n\n**Common Approaches:**\n- **Approach A (Full Build):** Complete implementation across all segments\n- **Approach B (Phased Rollout):** Start with one segment, expand\n- **Approach C (Quick Win):** Minimum viable implementation first\n\n**Decision Criteria:**\n- Timeline and urgency\n- Available resources\n- Data readiness\n- Organizational change capacity\n",
    "implementation": "# Quote-to-Cash — Implementation\n\n> **PLACEHOLDER** — This content is under development.\n\n## Part 3: Build & Configure\n\n### Step 6: CRM Configuration\n\n- Create or modify required custom fields\n- Build automation rules (Flows, Workflows)\n- Configure validation rules\n- Set up record types if needed\n- Test in sandbox before production\n\n### Step 7: Integration Setup\n\n- Connect required third-party tools\n- Configure API connections and webhooks\n- Set up data sync schedules\n- Validate data flow end-to-end\n- Document integration architecture\n\n### Step 8: Reporting & Dashboards\n\n**Key Metrics to Track:**\n\n| Metric | Definition | Target | Frequency |\n|--------|-----------|--------|-----------|\n| [Metric 1] | [How it's measured] | [Benchmark] | Weekly |\n| [Metric 2] | [How it's measured] | [Benchmark] | Monthly |\n| [Metric 3] | [How it's measured] | [Benchmark] | Quarterly |\n\n- Build executive dashboard with KPIs\n- Create operational reports for daily management\n- Set up automated report delivery\n- Configure alerts for metric thresholds\n\n## Part 4: Launch & Enable\n\n### Step 9: User Acceptance Testing\n\n- Define test scenarios covering all workflows\n- Recruit test users from each stakeholder group\n- Execute test plan and document results\n- Fix critical issues before go-live\n- Get sign-off from project sponsor\n\n### Step 10: Training & Rollout\n\n**Training Plan:**\n- Admin training (RevOps team) — 2 hours\n- End user training (Sales/Marketing) — 1 hour\n- Quick reference guide distributed\n- Office hours for first 2 weeks post-launch\n\n### Step 11: Post-Launch Support\n\n- Monitor adoption metrics for first 30 days\n- Weekly check-ins with stakeholders\n- Address issues and edge cases\n- Document learnings and process refinements\n- Transition to steady-state operations\n"
  },
