    "implementation": "# Website Lead Capture and Form Compliance — Implementation\n\n> **PLACEHOLDER** — This content is under development.\n\n## Part 3: Build & Configure\n\n### Step 6: CRM Configuration\n\n- Create or modify required custom fields\n- Build automation rules (Flows, Workflows)\n- Configure validation rules\n- Set up record types if needed\n- Test in sandbox before production\n\n### Step 7: Integration Setup\n\n- Connect required third-party tools\n- Configure API connections and webhooks\n- Set up data sync schedules\n- Validate data flow end-to-end\n- Document integration architecture\n\n### Step 8: Reporting & Dashboards\n\n**Key Metrics to Track:**\n\n| Metric | Definition | Target | Frequency |\n|--------|-----------|--------|-----------|\n| [Metric 1] | [How it's measured] | [Benchmark] | Weekly |\n| [Metric 2] | [How it's measured] | [Benchmark] | Monthly |\n| [Metric 3] | [How it's measured] | [Benchmark] | Quarterly |\n\n- Build executive dashboard with KPIs\n- Create operational reports for daily management\n- Set up automated report delivery\n- Configure alerts for metric thresholds\n\n## Part 4: Launch & Enable\n\n### Step 9: User Acceptance Testing\n\n- Define test scenarios covering all workflows\n- Recruit test users from each stakeholder group\n- Execute test plan and document results\n- Fix critical issues before go-live\n- Get sign-off from project sponsor\n\n### Step 10: Training & Rollout\n\n**Training Plan:**\n- Admin training (RevOps team) — 2 hours\n- End user training (Sales/Marketing) — 1 hour\n- Quick reference guide distributed\n- Office hours for first 2 weeks post-launch\n\n### Step 11: Post-Launch Support\n\n- Monitor adoption metrics for first 30 days\n- Weekly check-ins with stakeholders\n- Address issues and edge cases\n- Document learnings and process refinements\n- Transition to steady-state operations\n",
